.env
# Any sidecar of .env -- backups, rotations, per-environment copies. A
# .env.bak-* holding two live tokens existed on 2026-10-19 and this file
# would NOT have ignored it; the hygiene gate caught it instead. The
# same suffix blind spot already bit once before. .env.example is
# re-allowed because it is the one committed template. B-22.
.env.*
!.env.example
_secrets/
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# Terraform. terraform.tfvars carries a workspace PAT, and tfstate
# carries every value Terraform read -- including the token, in
# cleartext, which is why the state file is ignored by name rather than
# trusted to be clean. terraform.tfvars.example IS committed: it is the
# template, and it holds placeholders only.
iac/databricks/terraform.tfvars
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
